5,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,Let’s start with the basics. What are the four plans actually proposing for the central park?,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Misaki,,I don’t have the plan details yet. We should review the documents before discussing specifics.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Mio,,I’m excited to see what’s possible! I just want to make sure we don’t fall in love with pretty pictures that break the budget later.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Asuka,,I’m focused on the operational reality. Who is actually staffing the maintenance rota once the ribbon is cut?,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Minako,,I’m concerned about how the design fits the actual ground and daily use. Let’s see the proposals before we judge.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, your budget worry is valid, but I’d rather look at the condition of our earlier works first.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The ground conditions and contractor capacity are critical. I’ll check the earth-moving tenders and the earlier works.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
