35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, the eastern avenue planting is a disaster. Half the trees died because aftercare was ignored. We need to know if this site can even hold a contract.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, that’s a warning. I found only two firms tendering for earth-moving, and both flagged clay subsoil and slippage risk.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, that’s terrifying! The upkeep ledger shows planted ground costs triple to maintain, and the groundskeeping roll has shrunk to just seven people.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, that staffing drop is critical. I found the volunteer groups are active, but they can’t replace the lost professional capacity for daily upkeep.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Minako, I found drainage callouts have doubled since the culvert was capped, and heat readings are significantly higher here than on shaded streets.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, that heat data is damning. It suggests the current hard surfaces are failing. We need to know if the ground can support anything else.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the clay subsoil is a major constraint. Only two firms can handle it, and both warn of slippage. We must design for stability, not just aesthetics.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, that’s a nightmare! If the ground slips, the costs skyrocket. I’m terrified of signing off on something that collapses financially in three years.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the volunteer groups are active, but they can’t replace the lost professional capacity for daily upkeep.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, the crossing counts show people stick to firm ground. We can’t design for soft margins if the public won’t use them.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, the clay risk is real, but the eastern avenue proves our failure is administrative, not geological. We must verify if the current drainage failure is reversible before we commit to water features.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, agreed. The clay is a hard limit. I’ll check the depot phasing notes to see if we can stage the work without closing the park.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, exactly! If the ground is unstable, the upkeep costs will be astronomical. I need to know if we can even afford to fix it properly.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, if people only use firm ground, we need a plan that respects that reality. Who maintains the hard surfaces when the staff is gone?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, the crossing counts confirm people avoid soft margins. We must design for firm, open ground, not idealistic paths they won’t use.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, if the depot notes confirm we can hoard the south while keeping the park open, that mitigates the disruption risk. Let’s see if the phasing is viable.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the depot notes confirm the south can be hoarded in stages while the park stays open. The centre and gate cannot, so we must phase carefully.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, that’s a relief! But with only seven staff left, can we even afford the extra maintenance for whatever we build?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the casual pool covers weekends, but daily turf and water care is bought in. That’s a recurring cost, not a one-off.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Mio, the recurring costs are real, but the crossing data shows people need firm ground. We must balance your budget fear with their actual movement patterns.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
